    "details": "R. Elliott Childre reports:\n\n> The clone() method of the identification_t class doesn\\'t correctly\n> handle identities that have an empty but non-NULL encoding. Both\n> objects will point to the same location, resulting in a double-free\n> once the second object is destroyed. This can lead to a crash and\n> could potentially be exploitable for remote code execution. Affected\n> are all strongSwan versions since 4.3.3.\n",
    "id": "FreeBSD-2026-0243",
